`blkI pM`: with a block header `[n, 2n, kG b (2n) 2^pk, (2^b)^(4n)]` and the block tables `am, ap`
on top of the table stack `dT`, the four stage tables on `TDI, TGI, TGA, TDD`, and the block
input `z` (length `n`) on top of the row stack `0`, it pushes `gflat (blkG …).reverse` onto `OUT`,
consumes the header and tables from `dT` onto the consumed-descriptor stack `DU`, and decrements
the block counter `BC`.

The stacks the block body changes are kept in the frame `BF` (twelve stacks over a base `G`).
-/

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
